meta {
  name: Who is expected in maths on Monday
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/register?subject_offering_id={{offeringId}}&period_id={{periodOneId}}&attendance_date=2026-11-02
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.class.in_session: eq true
  res.body.class.scheduled: eq true
  res.body.class.cancelled: eq false
  res.body.class.half: eq forenoon
  res.body.count: eq 0
  res.body.section_id: eq {{sectionId}}
}

docs {
  Read this before writing, because the class block is the only place the
  reason a register will be refused is visible before it is refused. in_session
  comes from the calendar day, scheduled from whether an occurrence for that
  offering and period stands on the date, cancelled from a deviation. All
  three true and not cancelled is the only combination POST will accept.

  state is "relocated" here rather than "planned" because folder 12 moved this
  class to another room for the day. A relocated class still takes a register.

  It answers 200 with count 0 before anything is marked, rather than 404. An
  unmarked register is a fact about the class, not a missing resource.
}
